    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d643">

                <pb facs="0640" n="634" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg634"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr. von Holleben.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-03-10"><hi rendition="#italic">March 10,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. von Mumm’s note of the 3d
                    instant, relative to the action of your Government in authorizing the acting
                    imperial consul at Apia to select a person to act provisionally as land
                    commissioner until the arrival of the commissioner who is soon to be appointed,
                    I have the honor to inform you that this Government accepts the temporary
                    expedient in the expectation that the permanent appointment of Mr. Eggert’s
                    successor will be made as soon as possible.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
